WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.424
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Stop and Go Brain Builder.

00:00:12.424 --> 00:00:16.849
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.504
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:19.504 --> 00:00:22.158
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.158 --> 00:00:30.122
We are going to build a strong stop-and-go brain.

00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:38.087
When I say go, we move — small and gentle, right in our seats.

00:00:38.087 --> 00:00:43.396
When I say stop, everything freezes. Body still. Breath soft and easy.

00:00:43.396 --> 00:00:46.935
Stopping is a skill, like a muscle. Every stop makes it stronger.

00:00:46.935 --> 00:00:54.015
Round one: wiggle your fingers. Ready? Go… wiggle, wiggle, wiggle.

00:00:54.015 --> 00:01:00.209
And stop. Freeze. Fingers still.

00:01:00.209 --> 00:01:06.403
Feel that? Your whole body listened. That listening is the stop muscle working.

00:01:06.403 --> 00:01:12.598
Go again… wiggle, wiggle.

00:01:12.598 --> 00:01:18.792
And stop. Still as a statue. One soft breath… and let it go.

00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:26.756
Round two: roll your shoulders, slow and round. Go… roll, roll, roll.

00:01:26.756 --> 00:01:33.835
And stop. Shoulders melt down. Everything quiet.

00:01:33.835 --> 00:01:40.029
Round three: tap your knees, soft as rain. Go… tap, tap, tap.

00:01:40.029 --> 00:01:45.339
And stop. Hands resting on your desk. Body still.

00:01:45.339 --> 00:01:51.533
Now the strongest round of all: the still round. Nothing moves. Just breathing, slow and easy.

00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:58.612
You can start. You can stop. You can stay. Your brain is getting stronger every round.

00:01:58.612 --> 00:02:01.267
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:04.806
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:04.806 --> 00:02:08.346
You're ready for what's next.
